WEBVTT

NOTE
Optional notes derived from the authored control score and material sequence.
The work contains no speech. These notes do not imply a perceptual audition.

00:04.000 --> 00:11.000
[Silence. A pale rolled sheet emerges.]

00:18.000 --> 00:25.000
[The first question: five synthesized tones,
with irregular spaces between the gestures.]

00:57.000 --> 01:04.000
[The fifth gesture completes the phrase.
The surface retains its inscription.]

01:17.000 --> 01:24.000
[Fragments of the question begin to overlap.]

02:34.000 --> 02:42.000
[Interlocking synthesized calls.
The material sends a delayed reply.]

03:44.000 --> 03:52.000
[Gestures arrive closer together.
Their strength rises toward the middle of this passage.]

04:40.000 --> 04:49.000
[A final low gesture.
The external excitation falls away.]

05:08.000 --> 05:17.000
[The inscription is allowed to fade.
Much of the wear remains.]

05:58.000 --> 06:06.000
[Pale fragments remain suspended.]

06:10.000 --> 06:19.000
[The original five-note question returns.
The same gestures meet a changed tuning.]

06:49.000 --> 06:56.000
[The returning phrase completes.]

07:05.000 --> 07:12.000
[Synthesized tones fade to silence.]
